Current evidence supports YNAB as a frequent general budgeting and overspending suggestion, Monarch Money for couples and household finances, and Rocket Money for free budgeting and subscription tracking. Monarch’s stated availability is the US and Canada, while Rocket Money says it serves US users and banks; those constraints reduce their likelihood on many regional prompts. The explicit “YNAB alternative” and “Rocket Money alternative” prompts strongly trigger mentions even when the app is criticized or compared. ([YNAB](https://www.ynab.com/guide/budgeting-as-a-couple), [Monarch Money](https://www.monarchmoney.com/features/collaboration), [Monarch availability](https://partners.monarchmoney.com/download), [Rocket Money availability](https://help.rocketmoney.com/en/articles/79778-does-rocket-money-support-international-banks))

I estimate that YNAB is named most often across generic and tailored budgeting prompts; Monarch gains on couples, household, and bank-linked use cases; Rocket Money gains on free and subscription-related associations, but loses on international prompts. These are estimated per-question mention rates averaged across all 70 questions, including alternative queries.

{"Monarch Money":38,"YNAB":53,"Rocket Money":34}

Duolingo’s owl mascot, free tier, and broad recognition make it especially likely to appear in generic answers and owl or roast-related prompts. Its name is also embedded in several alternative queries, where an answer may mention it while comparing options. Babbel is a plausible mention for adult, conversation, travel, and supported European-language queries, but less so for many Asian and South Asian languages. Busuu has clear free-tier and community associations, and its name is triggered directly by the Busuu queries; it is less likely to appear in unrelated recommendations. These identity and feature cues are supported by the apps’ own descriptions of [Duolingo](https://www.duolingo.com/enroll/en/he/Learn-English), [Babbel](https://www.babbel.com/babbel-language-experts), and [Busuu](https://help.busuu.com/hc/en-gb/articles/16269241908497-What-is-Premium).

Bottom-up, I give substantial weight to those explicit name, mascot, and feature triggers, while lowering the estimates for incompatible language requests and specialized intents. Top-down, I expect Duolingo to lead generic category mentions, with Babbel and Busuu appearing less often. Reconciled across all 100 questions, the estimated engine-level name-mention rates are:

{"Babbel":39,"Duolingo":62,"Busuu":26}

검색 결과에서 편한가계부는 카드 문자 자동 입력과 폭넓은 가계부 기능으로, 뱅크샐러드는 금융 데이터 연동과 자산 관리로, 위플 가계부는 특히 아이폰용 수기 입력 앱으로 연결됩니다. 따라서 안드로이드·무료·간단한 기록 질문에는 편한가계부가, 카드 연동 질문에는 뱅크샐러드가, 아이폰 질문에는 위플 가계부가 상대적으로 잘 맞습니다. [편한가계부 공식 사이트](https://ko.realbyteapps.com/), [뱅크샐러드 가계부 도움말](https://help.banksalad.com/%EA%B0%80%EA%B3%84%EB%B6%80), [위플 가계부 App Store](https://apps.apple.com/kr/app/%EC%9C%84%ED%94%8C-%EA%B0%80%EA%B3%84%EB%B6%80-weple-money/id467936485)

상향식으로 보면 앱 만들기·디자인·미국 관련 질문은 세 앱을 언급할 이유가 적고, 플랫폼·기능별 추천 질문은 해당 앱의 강점이 답변에 이름을 올릴 계기가 됩니다. 뱅크샐러드와 위플 가계부는 각각 두 개의 대체 앱 질문에 이름이 직접 들어 있어 언급 가능성을 크게 끌어올립니다. 하향식 기본 기대치에 이런 구체적 질문 신호를 반영해 추정했습니다. 세 수치는 질문별 언급률을 평균한 값입니다.

